            "key_investigations.3",
            "key_investigations.4",
            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4",
            "treatment.5"
          ],
          "text": "On admission he was febrile (38.6), tachypnoeic (respiratory rate 26) and hypoxic (saturations 89% on room air) with coarse crackles at the right base. Chest X-ray confirmed right lower lobe consolidation; CRP was 180 and white cell count 16. He was treated with IV co-amoxiclav, IV clarithromycin, controlled oxygen therapy and IV fluids. ITU review was undertaken on Day 2, at which point a ceiling of care was agreed as ward-based given his COPD severity and frailty. He was stepped down to oral antibiotics on Day 3 (10/05) and was discharged on 12/05 with oxygen saturations of 93% on room air.",
