        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came in with a cough with phlegm, a fever and breathlessness. These had been going on for 4 days.\n\nThe team found you had a chest infection called pneumonia (community-acquired pneumonia). This is an infection in the lungs. You also have a background of:\n- A lung condition (COPD)\n- An irregular heartbeat (atrial fibrillation)\n- High blood pressure (hypertension)"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "When you arrived, your temperature was high and your oxygen levels were low. A chest X-ray showed an infection in the lower right part of your lung.\n\nYou were given:\n- Antibiotics through a drip (co-amoxiclav and clarithromycin)\n- Controlled oxygen therapy\n- Fluids through a drip\n\nOn Day 3 (10/05) you were switched to antibiotic tablets.\n\nBy Day 5, your oxygen levels had risen."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7",
            "sections.8"
          ],
          "text": "- You have a respiratory clinic appointment in 6 weeks.\n- Your GP will review your COPD inhaler technique."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.4",
          "heading": "safety_net",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{SAFETY_NET}}"
        }
